Uh-oh, sorry! - Too many cryptic words.

NAO is the publich server nethack.alt.org that allows others
to view the active games played via telnet on that server.

And DiamondRobin is one specific account defined to allow
players of approx. equal skill to play on the same game.
Every participant shall not make more than around 1000
moves and save the game then. Other players may continue.
The idea is, if someone just wants to play a bit and does not
want to play a whole game alone, he can join for a while.
Playing a *Robin game requires some ingame bookkeeping
(use of the name-command) to pass information for subsequent
players.

At the time it had been invented there were the accounts
RoundRobin, SquareRobin, and DiamondRobin, with increased
skill demands. Lastly there are some more (closed usergroup)
Robin accounts on NAO.

